  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Woman and Man** (1 review): Listener calls this track and Awesome Sound ridiculous, highlighting Deaner's performance [5]\n- **Stay Forever** (1 review): Listener notes the joy of receiving this acoustic song in the set [5]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Buenos Tardes Amigos**: rare: 11 archived performances [6]\n- **Squeal on the Pusher**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **Claude**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween2008-07-17.Flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 33 songs; 166 min; rated 4/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Audio is described as muddy, chatty, and bottom-heavy, typical of the venue [5]\n- **ween2008-07-17.ca11**: source not stated; 33 songs; 162 min [3]\n- **ween2008-07-17.mbho603a.ka200n.pmd-671**: source not stated; 33 songs; 166 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Band attempted to restart Squeal, but Claude soloed until destroying his drumkit [3]\n- Listener claims the performance goes down in history, signaling a strong return [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween2008-07-17.Flac16**: taped by simpdawg; transferred by simpdawg; source: MBHO603A/KA200N (OTS/DFC/DIN) > Segue Dogstar Silver XLR > Busman-mod Marantz PMD-671 > 24-bit/96kHz WAV [1]\n- **ween2008-07-17.ca11**: taped by Chris King; transferred by Chris King; source: Church-Audio STC-11> Church-Audio ST-9100 > M-audio2 (24/96) [3]. Also: Recorded via Church-Audio STC-11 and ST-9100, transferred from CF card to FLAC [3]\n- **ween2008-07-17.mbho603a.ka200n.pmd-671**: taped by simpdawg; transferred by simpdawg; source: MBHO603A/KA200N (OTS/DFC/DIN) > Segue Dogstar Silver XLR > Busman-mod Marantz PMD-671 > 24-bit/96kHz WAV [2]",
